    <name>
      <text>Find percentiles_c</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find \(P_{@index_1@} \) and \(P_{@index_2@} \) for the following frequency distribution where  \(P_{n}\) denotes the \(n^{th}\) percentile.</p>
<p>Hint: Express your final answer in exact form where necessary, otherwise in 1 decimal place.</p>
<p>
<table border="solid">
  <tr>
    <th width="25%", style="text-align:center">Weight</th>
    <th width="25%", style="text-align:center">Frequency</th>
    <th width="30%", style="text-align:center">Cum.fr</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@w1_l@}-{@w1_r@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@freq_1@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">{@cum_freq1@}</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <td style="text-align:center">\({@w2_l@}-{@w2_r@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@freq_2@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
     <td style="text-align:center">\({@w3_l@}-{@w3_r@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@freq_3@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <td style="text-align:center">\({@w4_l@}-{@w4_r@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@freq_4@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</td>
  </tr>
  </table>
</p>
<p> \(P_{@index_1@}=\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>
<p>  \(P_{@index_2@}=\)[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b><h3>Worked solution</h3></b></p>
<p>
<table border="solid">
  <tr>
    <th width="25%", style="text-align:center">Weight</th>
    <th width="25%", style="text-align:center">Frequency</th>
    <th width="30%", style="text-align:center">Cum.fr</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@w1_l@}-{@w1_r@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@freq_1@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">{@cum_freq1@}</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <td style="text-align:center">\({@w2_l@}-{@w2_r@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@freq_2@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">{@cum_freq2@}</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
     <td style="text-align:center">\({@w3_l@}-{@w3_r@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@freq_3@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">{@cum_freq3@}</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <td style="text-align:center">\({@w4_l@}-{@w4_r@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@freq_4@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">{@cum_freq4@}</td>
  </tr>
  </table>
</p>
<p> \(P_{@index_1@}= \left( \displaystyle \frac{{@index_1@} \times {@cum_freq4@}}{100}\right)^{@th@}\) item = \((\displaystyle {@p_index1@})^{th}\), which is in the \( {@class_wrt_index1@}^{@exponent1_class@} \) class.
<br> So  \(P_{@index_1@}=\displaystyle {@bd_wrt_index1@}+ \left( \displaystyle \frac{{@p_index1@}-{@choix_cumfreq_class@}}{@choix_freq_den@} \right) \times {@w_th@} ={@sol1@}\)</p>
<hr>
<p> \(P_{@index_2@}= \left( \displaystyle \frac{{@index_2@} \times {@cum_freq4@}}{100}\right)^{th}\) item = \((\displaystyle {@p_index2@})^{th}\), which is in the \( {@class_wrt_index2@}^{@exponent2_class@} \) class.
<br> So  \(P_{@index_2@}= \displaystyle {@bd_wrt_index2@}+ \left(\displaystyle \frac{{@p_index2@}-{@choix_cumfreq_class_s@}}{@choix_freq_den_s@} \right) \times {@w_th@} ={@sol2@}\)</p.]]></text>
